Supreme People's Court

Notice on Issuing the Provisions on Strictly Regulating the Conclusion of Enforcement Cases by the Procedure of "Termination of This Enforcement Procedure" (Trial Implementation)

Fa [2016] No. 373

High People's Courts of all provinces, autonomous regions, and municipalities directly under the Central Government; the Military Court of the People's Liberation Army; the Production and Construction Corps Branch of the High People's Court of Xinjiang Uygur Autonomous Region:

The Provisions on Strictly Regulating the Conclusion of Enforcement Cases by the Procedure of "Termination of This Enforcement Procedure" (Trial Implementation) of the Supreme People's Court are hereby issued for your earnest implementation.

October 29, 2016

Provisions on Strictly Regulating the Conclusion of Enforcement Cases by the Procedure of "Termination of This Enforcement Procedure" (Trial Implementation)

For the purpose of strictly regulating the conclusion of enforcement cases by the procedure of "termination of this enforcement procedure" and safeguarding the lawful rights and interests of the parties, these Provisions are formulated in accordance with the Civil Procedure Law of the People's Republic of China and the provisions of relevant judicial interpretations, and in light of the actual circumstances of the enforcement work of the people's courts.

Article 1 When a people's court concludes an enforcement case by the procedure of "termination of this enforcement procedure," the following conditions shall be concurrently satisfied:

(1) A notice of enforcement has been issued to the judgment debtor and an order to report property has been made;

(2) An order restricting consumption has been issued to the judgment debtor, and the judgment debtor who meets the conditions has been included in the list of dishonest judgment debtors;

(3) Property investigation measures have been exhausted, and no property of the judgment debtor available for enforcement has been found, or the discovered property cannot be disposed of;

(4) More than three months have elapsed since the date of case filing for enforcement;

(5) If the whereabouts of the judgment debtor are unknown, a lawful search has been conducted; if the judgment debtor or any other person has obstructed enforcement, compulsory measures such as fine and detention have been lawfully imposed; if the conduct constitutes a crime, the procedure for investigating criminal liability has been lawfully initiated.

Article 2 The "order to report property" referred to in item (1) of Article 1 of these Provisions means that the following matters shall be completed:

(1) An order to report property has been issued to the judgment debtor;

(2) The property reported by the judgment debtor has been verified;

(3) For the judgment debtor or relevant persons who fail to report within the time limit, refuse to report, or make false reports, compulsory measures such as fine and detention have been lawfully imposed; if the conduct constitutes a crime, the procedure for investigating criminal liability has been lawfully initiated.

The people's court shall record the circumstances of property reporting, verification, and punishment in the case file.

Article 3 The phrase "property investigation measures have been exhausted" referred to in item (3) of Article 1 of these Provisions means that the following investigation matters shall have been completed:

(1) Verification of property leads provided by the judgment creditor or other persons;

(2) Inquiry into the property of the judgment debtor, including deposits, vehicles and other means of transportation, immovable property, negotiable securities, etc., through the online enforcement investigation and control system;

(3) Where the property circumstances specified in item (2) of this paragraph cannot be inquired through the online enforcement investigation and control system, a necessary investigation shall be conducted at the place of the judgment debtor's domicile or at a place where property may be concealed or transferred;

(4) Where the judgment debtor conceals property, accounting books, or other materials and refuses to hand them over, search measures have been lawfully taken;

(5) Upon application by the judgment debtor, and based on the actual circumstances of the case, investigation measures such as audit investigation and public reward offers have been lawfully taken;

(6) Other property investigation measures provided for by laws and judicial interpretations.

The people's court shall record the circumstances of property investigation in the case file.

Article 4 The phrase "the discovered property cannot be disposed of" referred to in item (3) of Article 1 of these Provisions includes the following circumstances:

(1) The property of the judgment debtor has not been sold through auction or sale in accordance with statutory procedures, the judgment debtor does not accept satisfaction of debt by the property, or the property cannot be delivered to the judgment debtor for satisfaction of debt by law, and no other enforcement measures such as compulsory management can be taken against the property;

(2) Vehicles, vessels, or other property of the judgment debtor that have been sealed up or seized by the people's court at the registration authority cannot be actually taken into custody.

Article 5 Before concluding an enforcement case by the procedure of "termination of this enforcement procedure," the people's court shall inform the judgment creditor of the enforcement status of the case, the property investigation measures taken, the property circumstances of the judgment debtor, the basis and legal consequences of concluding the case by the procedure of "termination of this enforcement procedure," and shall hear the judgment creditor's opinions on such conclusion.

The people's court shall record the opinions of the judgment creditor in the case file.

Article 6 A written ruling shall be made for concluding an enforcement case by the procedure of "termination of this enforcement procedure," which shall state the following:

(1) The circumstances of the debt applied for enforcement;

(2) The enforcement process and the enforcement measures and compulsory measures taken;

(3) The property circumstances of the judgment debtor as ascertained;

(4) The debt circumstances realized;

(5) The judgment creditor's right to require the judgment debtor to continue performing the debt and to apply to the people's court for resumption of enforcement in accordance with law, and the judgment debtor's obligation to continue performing the debt to the judgment creditor.

After the written ruling concluding the case by the procedure of "termination of this enforcement procedure" is served on the judgment creditor, the enforcement case may be treated as closed. When conducting relevant statistics, the people's court shall distinguish cases closed by the procedure of "termination of this enforcement procedure" from cases closed by other methods.

The written ruling concluding the case by the procedure of "termination of this enforcement procedure" shall be publicly disclosed on the internet in accordance with law.

Article 7 If a party or interested person considers that the conclusion of the enforcement case by the procedure of "termination of this enforcement procedure" violates legal provisions, it may raise an objection to enforcement. The people's court shall examine the objection in accordance with the provisions of Article 225 of the Civil Procedure Law.

Article 8 After the enforcement case is concluded by the procedure of "termination of this enforcement procedure," the judgment debtor shall continue to perform the obligations determined in the effective legal instrument. If the judgment debtor voluntarily performs the obligations in full, the parties shall promptly inform the enforcement court.

Article 9 After the enforcement case is concluded by the procedure of "termination of this enforcement procedure," if the judgment creditor discovers that the judgment debtor has property available for enforcement, it may apply to the enforcement court for resumption of enforcement. The application for resumption of enforcement shall not be subject to the limitation period for application for enforcement. If the enforcement court verifies the circumstances and finds them true, it shall resume enforcement.

Within five years after the enforcement case is concluded by the procedure of "termination of this enforcement procedure," the enforcement court shall, every six months, inquire into the property of the judgment debtor through the online enforcement investigation and control system and inform the judgment debtor of the inquiry results. If the conditions for resumption of enforcement are satisfied, the enforcement court shall promptly resume enforcement.

Article 10 After the enforcement case is concluded by the procedure of "termination of this enforcement procedure," if it is found that the judgment debtor has property available for enforcement and failure to take enforcement measures immediately may result in the transfer, concealment, sale, or damage of the property, the enforcement court may, upon application by the judgment debtor or ex officio, immediately take control measures such as sealing up, seizure, and freezing.

Article 11 If a case satisfies the conditions for conclusion by the procedure of "termination of this enforcement procedure" and also satisfies the relevant provisions for transfer for bankruptcy review, the enforcement court shall, at the same time as making a ruling to conclude the case by the procedure of "termination of this enforcement procedure," transfer the relevant materials of the enforcement case to the people's court of the place of domicile of the judgment debtor for bankruptcy review.

Article 12 After the written ruling concluding the enforcement case by the procedure of "termination of this enforcement procedure" is served on the judgment creditor, the enforcement court shall, within seven days, enter the relevant case information into the information database of cases concluded by the procedure of "termination of this enforcement procedure" established by the Supreme People's Court, and shall publicly disclose the information to the public through that database in a unified manner.

Article 13 The information recorded in the information database of cases concluded by the procedure of "termination of this enforcement procedure" shall include the following:

(1) If the judgment debtor is a legal person or other organization: its name, place of domicile, organizational code, and the name of its legal representative or responsible person; if the judgment debtor is a natural person: his or her name, gender, age, identity document number, and address;

(2) The issuing authority and document number of the effective legal instrument, the enforcement case number, the case filing date, and the enforcement court;

(3) The obligations determined in the effective legal instrument and the performance status of the judgment debtor;

(4) Other matters deemed necessary to be recorded by the people's court.

Article 14 If a party or interested person considers that the published information of a case concluded by the procedure of "termination of this enforcement procedure" is erroneous, it may apply to the enforcement court for correction. If the enforcement court verifies the circumstances and finds them true, it shall make corrections within three days.

Article 15 After the enforcement case is concluded by the procedure of "termination of this enforcement procedure," the enforcement measures and compulsory measures lawfully taken by the people's court against the judgment debtor shall remain valid.

Article 16 After the enforcement case is concluded by the procedure of "termination of this enforcement procedure," if the judgment creditor applies for an extension of the term of sealing up, seizure, or freezing, the people's court shall handle the renewal of sealing up, seizure, or freezing procedures in accordance with law.

After the enforcement case is concluded by the procedure of "termination of this enforcement procedure," if a party or interested person applies for modification or addition of parties to the enforcement, and the statutory circumstances are met, the people's court shall support the application. If, after modification or addition of the judgment debtor, the judgment creditor applies for resumption of enforcement, the people's court shall support the application.

Article 17 After the enforcement case is concluded by the procedure of "termination of this enforcement procedure," if the judgment debtor or any other person obstructs enforcement, the people's court may impose a fine or detention in accordance with law; if the conduct constitutes a crime, criminal liability shall be investigated in accordance with law.

Article 18 Under any of the following circumstances, the people's court shall, within three days, remove the case information from the information database of cases concluded by the procedure of "termination of this enforcement procedure":

(1) The obligations determined in the effective legal instrument have been fully performed;

(2) Enforcement has been legally terminated by ruling;

(3) Other circumstances where removal is required by law.

Article 19 These Provisions shall come into effect as of December 1, 2016.
